*   Class is a blueprint for making an object.
*   Similarly Interfaces are blue prints for making a class.
*   An interface is a contract that specifies what a class must do, while the implementing class provides the actual implementation.
*   Interfaces can only have abstract methods and static constants.
*   A static constant is a value that is:
             static → shared by the whole class
             final → cannot be changed after initialization
             Syntax : static final + datatype + variable;

                     class Circle {
                         static final double PI = 3.14159;
                     }
             static → only one shared copy of PI
             final → PI's value cannot be changed
             You can access it directly using the class:
                     System.out.println(Circle.PI);

*   There are two main uses of Interfaces - To achieve multiple inheritance and achieve pure abstraction
*   Another classes implements interfaces
*   NOTE IMP - From JAVA 8 onwards Interfaces can have default and static methods as well.
*   In an interface, if you declare a method without default, static, or private, it is implicitly public abstract.
*   We can directly access Static method of any interface by using the interface name.
*   We can not directly use static methods of an interface using child class name
            Because interface static methods belong only to the interface itself and are not inherited by implementing classes.

*   Interface static methods are not inherited by implementing classes, but interface constants (public static final fields) are inherited and can be accessed using the implementing class name.

*   Default Method in Interface — Notes
    A default method is a method in an interface that has a method body/implementation.
    It is declared using the default keyword.
    It was introduced in Java 8.
    A default method is inherited by implementing classes.
    An implementing class does not have to override a default method.
    But the implementing class can override it if it needs different behavior.
    Default methods are instance methods, not static methods.
    They are called using an object of the implementing class.
    Main purpose: to provide common/default behavior to all implementing classes without forcing them to implement the method.

